From: Mritunjay Sharma <mritunjay.sharma@chainguard.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] Bug#39102340: build with OpenSSL 4.x

Backport of upstream MySQL Bug#39102340 (a0c866a7d6, c2cc9c1f44,
a045c23214) to percona-xtrabackup 8.4.0-5, taken from the mysql-8.4.11
backport in enterprise-packages/mysql/ (see mysql-8.4, #360701). The main
fix is cmake/ssl.cmake, which only accepted OpenSSL major version 3 and
so failed to configure against OpenSSL 4. Also carries the set_dh()
SSL_CTX_set_dh_auto() change from upstream 72e8989855 (WL#16504).

Hunks omitted from the mysql-8.4 backport:
- bundled curl and libfido2: this tree bundles older versions and the
  recipe builds against the system libraries.
- storage/ndb: NDB is not built (WITH_NDB defaults to OFF) and its
  compat header differs in this release.
- router/tests/component/test_bootstrap.cc: get_x509_name() does not
  exist in this release, and the router is not built.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/mysql/mysql-server/commit/a045c23214]
---
diff --git a/cmake/ssl.cmake b/cmake/ssl.cmake
index 932659d0..adcc5527 100644
--- a/cmake/ssl.cmake
+++ b/cmake/ssl.cmake
@@ -147,8 +147,8 @@ MACRO(FIND_OPENSSL_VERSION)
       ${version_part} "${${version_part}}")
   ENDFOREACH()
   SET(OPENSSL_VERSION_MAJOR ${OPENSSL_VERSION_MAJOR} CACHE INTERNAL "" FORCE)
-  IF(OPENSSL_VERSION_MAJOR VERSION_EQUAL 3)
-    # OpenSSL 3
+  IF(OPENSSL_VERSION_MAJOR VERSION_GREATER_EQUAL 3)
+    # OpenSSL >= 3
     SET(OPENSSL_FIX_VERSION "${OPENSSL_VERSION_PATCH}")
   ELSE()
     # Verify version number. Version information looks like:
